gain-split-zero.fixPlan:
In src/season.js splitProduct(before,after):
- Keep the current log-mean (LMDI) path when every factor is finite and > 0. Existing results and tests stay unchanged.
- If any factor is <= 0 but all are finite, return the exact 3-factor Shapley split. Average each factor's marginal contribution over the 6 orderings. In code:
  const f=s=>s.reduce((a,b)=>a*b,1),res=before.map(()=>0),orders=[[0,1,2],[0,2,1],[1,0,2],[1,2,0],[2,0,1],[2,1,0]];
  for(const o of orders){const cur=[...before];for(const i of o){const p=f(cur);cur[i]=after[i];res[i]+=(f(cur)-p)/orders.length;}}
  return res;
  The parts sum exactly to f(after)-f(before), stay finite at zeros, and handle negative perGame.
- Keep a [total,0,0] fallback only for non-finite factors.

explainSwap needs no change. It already rescales the parts to d, and the >half flags then fire correctly.

In docs/ACCEPTANCE.md:141, change the wording to: logarithmic mean for positive factors, and the Shapley average of the orderings when a player has no expected games or his club has no games in the period.

